  G. Orlanski et al., "SlopCodeBench: Benchmarking How Coding Agents Degrade Over
  Long-Horizon Iterative Tasks", arXiv:2603.24755.

Modifications: FUSE adapts the Circuit, CodeSearch and TextDrop task concepts into compact tasks,
each with a current requirement and two alternative futures. All requirements, starter repositories,
reference implementations, hidden test suites, scope boundaries and graders in benchmark/tasks were
written for FUSE. They are not SlopCodeBench problems, and results obtained with them are not
SlopCodeBench scores. The pinned upstream CITATION.cff (third_party/SlopCodeBench-CITATION.cff) states MIT;
the repository LICENSE (Apache-2.0) is treated as operative.

Mined development triples (mining/):
  mining/patches and mining/suites contain code and tests from Kludex/starlette
  (https://github.com/Kludex/starlette), BSD-3-Clause; see mining/patches/LICENSE-starlette.md.
  mining/strix/patches and mining/strix/suites contain code and tests from usestrix/strix
  (https://github.com/usestrix/strix), Apache-2.0; see mining/strix/patches/LICENSE-strix.txt.
  These files keep their upstream licences.

Credentials appearing in the TextDrop test suites (for example "password1") are synthetic test fixtures.
